1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,477
The outskirts of Hefei, in eastern China.
Winter.

2
00:00:03,477 --> 00:00:08,018
Two excavators are digging into the
ground. Police are watching.

3
00:00:08,568 --> 00:00:11,145
They dig for more than twenty hours.

4
00:00:11,145 --> 00:00:16,515
And six meters down, about twenty feet,
they find what they're looking for.

5
00:00:17,065 --> 00:00:22,200
More than eighty woven sacks. Inside, over
twelve hundred volumes of records.

6
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:27,201
According to Xinhua, China's state news
agency, suspects had buried them to

7
00:00:27,201 --> 00:00:28,601
destroy the evidence.

8
00:00:29,601 --> 00:00:35,168
The records belonged to a company that,
only months earlier, had been advertising

9
00:00:35,168 --> 00:00:37,092
on China's state television.

10
00:00:37,092 --> 00:00:42,590
Its name was Ezubao. And, a court would
later find, it and a sister platform had

11
00:00:42,590 --> 00:00:45,614
taken money from more than a million
people.

12
00:00:47,114 --> 00:00:52,461
The story starts in Bengbu, a mid-sized
city in Anhui Province, a few hours from

13
00:00:52,461 --> 00:00:53,062
Shanghai.

14
00:00:53,612 --> 00:00:59,006
There, a businessman named Ding Ning built
a group of companies called Yucheng.

15
00:00:59,006 --> 00:01:04,605
It started in manufacturing. Then, like
many ambitious firms in China in the early

16
00:01:04,605 --> 00:01:06,517
2010s, it turned to finance.

17
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:10,690
Those were the years of the peer-to-peer
lending boom.

18
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:15,789
The idea sounded modern. An app or a
website connects people with savings to

19
00:01:15,789 --> 00:01:17,600
businesses that need loans.

20
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:22,766
No bank in the middle. Higher returns for
savers. Faster money for borrowers.

21
00:01:23,016 --> 00:01:25,866
For ordinary savers, the timing was
perfect.

22
00:01:25,866 --> 00:01:30,853
Bank deposits paid little. The stock
market had just crashed in the summer of

23
00:01:30,853 --> 00:01:34,804
2015. People wanted somewhere safe that
still paid something.

24
00:01:35,054 --> 00:01:40,189
By late 2015, according to industry
counts, well over three thousand of these

25
00:01:40,189 --> 00:01:41,923
platforms had been set up.

26
00:01:41,923 --> 00:01:44,191
And regulation had barely started.

27
00:01:44,741 --> 00:01:52,516
According to Xinhua, in February 2014
Yucheng bought an internet finance company

28
00:01:52,516 --> 00:01:53,585
in Beijing.

29
00:01:53,585 --> 00:01:59,1000
In July 2014, it relaunched its platform
under a new name: Ezubao.

30
00:01:59,1000 --> 00:02:06,123
In Chinese, the name means something like
"e-leasing treasure."

31
00:02:06,373 --> 00:02:09,280
That word, leasing, was the whole pitch.

32
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:12,575
Here's how Ezubao said it worked.

33
00:02:12,575 --> 00:02:17,019
A real company needs equipment. Machinery,
vehicles, production lines.

34
00:02:17,019 --> 00:02:21,780
Yucheng's leasing company buys that
equipment and leases it to the company.

35
00:02:22,030 --> 00:02:26,857
To fund the deal, Ezubao sells pieces of
that lease to ordinary investors online.

36
00:02:26,857 --> 00:02:31,327
The company pays rent. The rent flows
back. And the investor gets a return.

37
00:02:31,877 --> 00:02:37,225
The court later found that these products,
with names like "Annual Enjoyment,"

38
00:02:37,225 --> 00:02:40,517
promised annual returns of nine to 14.6
percent.

39
00:02:40,517 --> 00:02:46,002
A one-year bank deposit in China paid far
less. The official benchmark rate fell

40
00:02:46,002 --> 00:02:48,539
from three percent to one and a half.

41
00:02:48,789 --> 00:02:53,653
And according to Chinese prosecutors, you
could start with just one yuan, about

42
00:02:53,653 --> 00:02:57,286
fifteen cents, and take your money out
whenever you wanted.

43
00:02:58,286 --> 00:02:59,904
Now here's how it actually worked.

44
00:03:00,454 --> 00:03:05,714
According to Xinhua's investigation,
Ezubao paid companies and middlemen for

45
00:03:05,714 --> 00:03:10,628
real companies' information. Their
registration papers. Their licenses.

46
00:03:10,878 --> 00:03:15,280
The head of risk control at Yucheng's
leasing arm told Xinhua that, on Ding

47
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:20,033
Ning's instructions, they paid one and a
half to two percent of the "loan" amount

48
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:21,618
for each company's details.

49
00:03:21,868 --> 00:03:26,470
His department then typed those details
into ready-made contracts and posted them

50
00:03:26,470 --> 00:03:28,174
online as investment projects.

51
00:03:28,174 --> 00:03:32,719
To make them look stronger, he said, they
even changed the companies' registered

52
00:03:32,719 --> 00:03:33,174
capital.

53
00:03:33,724 --> 00:03:39,808
His summary was blunt. "As far as I know,
95 percent of the projects on Ezubao were

54
00:03:39,808 --> 00:03:40,248
fake."

55
00:03:40,248 --> 00:03:45,893
Ding Ning himself told Xinhua that the
group spent more than 800 million yuan

56
00:03:45,893 --> 00:03:47,432
buying this material.

57
00:03:47,982 --> 00:03:52,781
Police said that of the 207 leasing
customers they had checked, only one had

58
00:03:52,781 --> 00:03:54,802
done real business with Yucheng.

59
00:03:54,802 --> 00:03:58,085
Some companies only found out when police
told them.

60
00:03:58,335 --> 00:04:04,219
One business owner told Xinhua that his
firm had once taken a bank loan through a

61
00:04:04,219 --> 00:04:09,812
Yucheng guarantee company. Then, in late
2015, his company's bank account was

62
00:04:09,812 --> 00:04:15,550
frozen, and police told him Ezubao had
listed his company online to raise money

63
00:04:15,550 --> 00:04:16,422
in its name.

64
00:04:16,972 --> 00:04:19,055
And who guaranteed these loans?

65
00:04:19,055 --> 00:04:24,565
According to Xinhua, Yucheng itself. It
controlled three guarantee companies and a

66
00:04:24,565 --> 00:04:28,058
factoring company that backed Ezubao's own
projects.

67
00:04:28,058 --> 00:04:32,829
Police said the investors' money went into
a pool the group controlled.

68
00:04:33,079 --> 00:04:38,464
Xinhua summed up the trick in three
phrases: fake projects, fake third

69
00:04:38,464 --> 00:04:40,387
parties, fake guarantees.

70
00:04:40,937 --> 00:04:47,293
Xinhua pointed out that, under guidelines
China's central bank and other regulators

71
00:04:47,293 --> 00:04:53,418
issued in July 2015, a lending platform
was supposed to be only a matchmaker. No

72
00:04:53,418 --> 00:04:56,481
pool of money of its own. No guarantees.

73
00:04:56,481 --> 00:04:58,166
Ezubao was doing both.

74
00:04:59,366 --> 00:05:02,785
So why did hundreds of thousands of people
trust it?

75
00:05:02,785 --> 00:05:05,875
Part of the answer is advertising. A lot
of it.

76
00:05:06,425 --> 00:05:11,980
According to the court's judgment, Ezubao
advertised on major TV channels across

77
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:15,937
China, in subway stations, airports and
railway stations.

78
00:05:15,937 --> 00:05:21,006
It even had a high-speed train named after
it: the "Ezubao" bullet train.

79
00:05:21,256 --> 00:05:26,254
Chinese media reported that its ads ran on
China Central Television, the state

80
00:05:26,254 --> 00:05:29,842
broadcaster, in prime time before the main
evening news.

81
00:05:30,392 --> 00:05:35,779
According to the judgment, it spent more
than 480 million yuan on advertising.

82
00:05:35,779 --> 00:05:37,851
About seventy million dollars.

83
00:05:38,401 --> 00:05:40,292
And it had a friendly expert.

84
00:05:40,292 --> 00:05:45,315
A financial commentator who appeared in
Chinese media joined the company and,

85
00:05:45,315 --> 00:05:50,402
according to Chinese reporting on the
judgment, spoke for Ezubao at forums and

86
00:05:50,402 --> 00:05:53,859
in interviews, vouching for it as an
industry expert.

87
00:05:54,109 --> 00:05:58,365
He was later convicted too, and sentenced
to four and a half years.

88
00:05:59,365 --> 00:06:01,114
Think about what that does.

89
00:06:01,114 --> 00:06:06,167
In China, state television isn't just
another channel. For many families, it's

90
00:06:06,167 --> 00:06:07,657
the voice of authority.

91
00:06:07,657 --> 00:06:12,839
If a company is on CCTV, on the bullet
train, in the airport, surely someone has

92
00:06:12,839 --> 00:06:13,552
checked it.

93
00:06:13,802 --> 00:06:19,607
After the collapse, investors reportedly
protested outside CCTV's headquarters in

94
00:06:19,607 --> 00:06:23,978
Beijing, saying those ads had helped
persuade them to invest.

95
00:06:24,529 --> 00:06:26,366
Ezubao also sold offline.

96
00:06:26,366 --> 00:06:32,317
According to Xinhua, the group ran eight
operating centers, including Beijing and

97
00:06:32,317 --> 00:06:36,137
Shanghai, and a nationwide network of
sales offices.

98
00:06:36,387 --> 00:06:41,589
Victims, the agency reported, were spread
across 31 provinces and regions. In

99
00:06:41,589 --> 00:06:43,211
practice, most of China.

100
00:06:44,411 --> 00:06:45,878
So where did the money go?

101
00:06:45,878 --> 00:06:50,563
The court's findings, based on a forensic
audit, answer that. And the answer is the

102
00:06:50,563 --> 00:06:52,200
definition of a Ponzi scheme.

103
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:58,640
The biggest share, about 38 billion yuan,
went straight back out as principal and

104
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:00,822
interest to earlier investors.

105
00:07:00,822 --> 00:07:02,858
New money, paying old money.

106
00:07:03,408 --> 00:07:07,196
The rest of the list reads like a
lifestyle.

107
00:07:07,196 --> 00:07:12,274
About 1.2 billion yuan given to senior
managers as "gifts."

108
00:07:12,274 --> 00:07:15,631
About 490 million yuan on luxury goods.

109
00:07:15,631 --> 00:07:20,624
About 920 million yuan on property,
aircraft and vehicles.

110
00:07:20,874 --> 00:07:25,691
And around 2.3 billion yuan moved abroad
as so-called investments.

111
00:07:26,241 --> 00:07:31,924
The court found that Ding Ning gave the
group's president, Zhang Min, assets worth

112
00:07:31,924 --> 00:07:33,587
around 700 million yuan.

113
00:07:33,587 --> 00:07:39,200
According to Xinhua, those gifts included
a villa in Singapore and a pink diamond

114
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:39,547
ring.

115
00:07:40,547 --> 00:07:44,319
The investors thought they were funding
factories and machinery.

116
00:07:44,319 --> 00:07:48,504
They were funding a carousel, and the
people at the top were riding it.

117
00:07:48,504 --> 00:07:52,806
And a carousel only keeps turning while
new riders keep paying to get on.

118
00:07:54,006 --> 00:08:00,320
Like every Ponzi scheme, Ezubao needed
more money coming in than going out. By

119
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:03,153
late 2015, that was getting harder.

120
00:08:03,703 --> 00:08:09,357
On December 3rd, 2015, according to
Chinese media, police took more than forty

121
00:08:09,357 --> 00:08:13,633
people from the platform's Shenzhen branch
for questioning.

122
00:08:13,633 --> 00:08:18,924
According to Xinhua, police later found
that by December 5th, the group's

123
00:08:18,924 --> 00:08:22,041
available cash was running dangerously
low.

124
00:08:22,291 --> 00:08:27,460
They also said Yucheng had started moving
money and destroying evidence, and that

125
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:30,077
several executives appeared ready to run.

126
00:08:30,627 --> 00:08:35,304
On December 8th, China's Ministry of
Public Security ordered a coordinated

127
00:08:35,304 --> 00:08:40,044
operation. Police across the country moved
on Ding Ning and the group's top

128
00:08:40,044 --> 00:08:40,740
executives.

129
00:08:40,740 --> 00:08:45,290
That same day, Xinhua announced that
Ezubao was under investigation. The

130
00:08:45,290 --> 00:08:46,491
platform went dark.

131
00:08:47,041 --> 00:08:49,310
For investors, the shock was total.

132
00:08:49,310 --> 00:08:54,562
Within days, according to foreign and Hong
Kong reports, investors were gathering

133
00:08:54,562 --> 00:08:59,230
outside company offices in several
provinces, and protesting in Beijing.

134
00:08:59,780 --> 00:09:05,658
On January 14th, 2016, Beijing prosecutors
approved the formal arrest of twenty-one

135
00:09:05,658 --> 00:09:07,641
people, including Ding Ning.

136
00:09:08,191 --> 00:09:12,441
Just over two weeks later, Xinhua
published its investigation.

137
00:09:12,441 --> 00:09:17,445
In a detention center, Zhang Min, the
group's president, told the agency,

138
00:09:17,445 --> 00:09:19,982
"Ezubao was a complete Ponzi scheme."

139
00:09:19,982 --> 00:09:24,780
She said senior management all knew it,
and that she was deeply sorry.

140
00:09:25,330 --> 00:09:28,429
And that's when the country learned about
the pit.

141
00:09:28,429 --> 00:09:33,634
Police told Xinhua the case was enormously
complex. More than two hundred servers to

142
00:09:33,634 --> 00:09:34,068
search.

143
00:09:34,318 --> 00:09:39,911
And the paper records? More than twelve
hundred volumes, in more than eighty

144
00:09:39,911 --> 00:09:43,222
sacks, six meters underground, outside
Hefei.

145
00:09:43,222 --> 00:09:46,092
Two excavators. More than twenty hours.

146
00:09:47,292 --> 00:09:52,649
In December 2016, Beijing prosecutors
filed charges against two Yucheng

147
00:09:52,649 --> 00:09:55,063
companies and twenty-six people.

148
00:09:55,613 --> 00:10:01,181
On September 12th, 2017, the Beijing No. 1
Intermediate People's Court delivered its

149
00:10:01,181 --> 00:10:01,711
verdict.

150
00:10:02,261 --> 00:10:08,848
The court found that from June 2014 to
December 2015, through Ezubao and a sister

151
00:10:08,848 --> 00:10:15,679
platform called Sesame Finance, the group
had used fake leasing and loan projects to

152
00:10:15,679 --> 00:10:18,444
take in more than 76 billion yuan.

153
00:10:18,694 --> 00:10:24,320
Strip out money that investors rolled over
and reinvested, and it was about 60

154
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:29,442
billion yuan, roughly nine billion
dollars, from more than 1.15 million

155
00:10:29,442 --> 00:10:29,947
people.

156
00:10:29,947 --> 00:10:34,563
More than 38 billion yuan, nearly six
billion dollars, was lost.

157
00:10:35,113 --> 00:10:40,433
Ding Ning was convicted of fundraising
fraud, smuggling precious metals,

158
00:10:40,433 --> 00:10:44,939
illegally possessing guns, and illegally
crossing the border.

159
00:10:44,939 --> 00:10:49,520
He was sentenced to life in prison and
fined 100 million yuan.

160
00:10:50,070 --> 00:10:55,229
His younger brother, Ding Dian, also a
senior executive, got life for fundraising

161
00:10:55,229 --> 00:10:55,611
fraud.

162
00:10:55,611 --> 00:11:00,516
Zhang Min and twenty-three others were
sentenced to between three and fifteen

163
00:11:00,516 --> 00:11:00,898
years.

164
00:11:01,448 --> 00:11:07,206
The two Yucheng companies were fined a
combined 1.9 billion yuan, about 290

165
00:11:07,206 --> 00:11:08,434
million dollars.

166
00:11:08,984 --> 00:11:14,625
In November 2017, the Beijing High
People's Court rejected the appeals. The

167
00:11:14,625 --> 00:11:16,205
sentences were final.

168
00:11:17,405 --> 00:11:21,611
But for the investors, the verdict didn't
answer the only question that mattered to

169
00:11:21,611 --> 00:11:21,864
them.

170
00:11:21,864 --> 00:11:23,486
How much of my money comes back?

171
00:11:24,036 --> 00:11:30,206
According to the judgment, as reported by
Chinese media, authorities had frozen

172
00:11:30,206 --> 00:11:36,219
almost 11 billion yuan in bank accounts,
and seized cash, property, vehicles,

173
00:11:36,219 --> 00:11:42,701
nearly 137 kilos of gold, and more than a
thousand pieces of jade, art and jewelry.

174
00:11:43,251 --> 00:11:44,927
Then came the waiting.

175
00:11:44,927 --> 00:11:51,022
In 2019, the Beijing court asked victims
nationwide to verify and register their

176
00:11:51,022 --> 00:11:51,555
losses.

177
00:11:51,555 --> 00:11:57,421
In January 2020, more than four years
after the platform went dark, the first

178
00:11:57,421 --> 00:11:58,792
payments went out.

179
00:11:59,042 --> 00:12:04,050
The court didn't publish the ratio, but
according to Chinese media and victims, it

180
00:12:04,050 --> 00:12:06,982
was about 35 percent of the money they had
lost.

181
00:12:07,532 --> 00:12:10,590
The second payout only came in April 2025.

182
00:12:10,590 --> 00:12:16,123
Again, the court gave no percentage.
Victims told Chinese reporters it added

183
00:12:16,123 --> 00:12:20,201
about five percent, bringing the total to
roughly forty.

184
00:12:20,201 --> 00:12:25,079
This time, former Ezubao employees were
included in the payout too.

185
00:12:26,079 --> 00:12:30,403
One investor told Chinese reporters,
quoted by the tech site KrASIA, that after

186
00:12:30,403 --> 00:12:33,852
more than four years he had almost
forgotten the money existed.

187
00:12:34,102 --> 00:12:39,556
Others had not forgotten for a single day.
According to foreign media reports at the

188
00:12:39,556 --> 00:12:44,426
time, many of the victims were small
investors, including families in rural

189
00:12:44,426 --> 00:12:46,763
areas, who had put in their savings.

190
00:12:47,313 --> 00:12:50,102
Forty cents on the yuan. After almost ten
years.

191
00:12:50,102 --> 00:12:53,181
For people who were promised fourteen
percent a year.

192
00:12:54,381 --> 00:12:59,006
Ezubao wasn't the only one. It was the
warning nobody fully heeded.

193
00:12:59,006 --> 00:13:04,321
Over the next few years, China's P2P
lending boom became a wave of collapses,

194
00:13:04,321 --> 00:13:06,392
defaults and runaway founders.

195
00:13:06,392 --> 00:13:10,396
Regulators tightened the rules, then shut
the sector down.

196
00:13:10,946 --> 00:13:16,287
In November 2020, China's banking
regulator said the number of P2P platforms

197
00:13:16,287 --> 00:13:20,082
had fallen from a peak of about five
thousand to zero.

198
00:13:20,332 --> 00:13:25,915
Three months earlier, its chairman had
said lenders were still owed more than 800

199
00:13:25,915 --> 00:13:30,120
billion yuan by failed platforms. Around
115 billion dollars.

200
00:13:30,670 --> 00:13:33,729
An entire industry, gone in about five
years.

201
00:13:33,729 --> 00:13:38,624
At its peak, according to Caixin, it had
around fifty million investors.

202
00:13:38,624 --> 00:13:41,819
Many of them are still waiting for their
money.

203
00:13:43,019 --> 00:13:47,889
Strip away the app and the bullet train,
and the shape is familiar.

204
00:13:47,889 --> 00:13:50,216
One. High returns, sold as safe.

205
00:13:50,216 --> 00:13:56,031
Two. A real-sounding business you can't
check. A lease on a machine you'll never

206
00:13:56,031 --> 00:13:56,322
see.

207
00:13:56,322 --> 00:14:00,247
Three. A promise you can take your money
out any time.

208
00:14:00,497 --> 00:14:04,128
Four. Credibility borrowed from
television, trains and experts.

209
00:14:04,128 --> 00:14:08,623
And five. A guarantee that, when you
follow the arrows, leads back to the same

210
00:14:08,623 --> 00:14:09,084
company.

211
00:14:10,084 --> 00:14:15,560
None of this is unique to China. The same
shape has turned up in Korea, in Vietnam,

212
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:17,737
across Asia and around the world.

213
00:14:17,737 --> 00:14:22,816
That's not investment advice. It's a
pattern. And a pattern is harder to bury

214
00:14:22,816 --> 00:14:23,542
than paper.

215
00:14:24,742 --> 00:14:29,523
Ezubao's real records weren't on a
website. They were in the ground.

216
00:14:29,523 --> 00:14:35,430
So when an investment promises safety, ask
one question: if you dug down six meters,

217
00:14:35,430 --> 00:14:36,836
what would you find?

218
00:14:37,386 --> 00:14:43,232
Next time: a country's own investment
fund. A superyacht, a Hollywood movie, and

219
00:14:43,232 --> 00:14:45,644
billions that simply disappeared.

220
00:14:46,194 --> 00:14:48,018
Subscribe so you don't miss it.

221
00:14:48,018 --> 00:14:52,902
And tell me in the comments: have you ever
trusted an investment because you saw it

222
00:14:52,902 --> 00:14:53,902
advertised on TV?

